{"skill":{"slug":"apple-notes","displayName":"Apple Notes"},"version":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1767545294031,"changelog":"","changelogSource":null,"license":null,"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":1883,"sha256":"493fde9a5e8df83739552821dc7902e086b1d6cca68b5f90ddf4b4a3488f37b6","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2060,"sha256":"a6f874bde3bcdf654be2c3fd5d34b6ebc01d7c0a50973a717f138ffe8cf67090","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789013574519,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"3a8836f1f9e514380be3a63ac1ef33ff55f359aeb352d3a0c5d2f9e829350bce","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/3a8836f1f9e514380be3a63ac1ef33ff55f359aeb352d3a0c5d2f9e829350bce","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: apple-notes\nVersion: 1.0.0\n\nThe skill bundle is designed to allow an AI agent to manage Apple Notes using the `memo` CLI tool. The `SKILL.md` provides standard installation instructions via Homebrew and clear usage examples for `memo notes` commands. There is no evidence of data exfiltration, malicious execution, persistence mechanisms, prompt injection attempts against the agent, or obfuscation. All described actions are directly related to the stated purpose of managing Apple Notes.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779159605492},"skillspector":{"status":"clean","normalizedStatus":"clean","score":9,"severity":"LOW","recommendation":"SAFE","issueCount":2,"checkedAt":1789013574519},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"This Apple Notes skill is purpose-aligned, but it asks users to install an unpinned third-party CLI and grant it access to sensitive Notes data with limited safety guidance.","dimensions":[{"detail":"macOS Automation access to Notes.app is expected for this purpose, but the skill under-explains that this grants terminal tooling access to read and modify Apple Notes content.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"Installation is delegated to a third-party Homebrew tap or a manual pip install from an unspecified cloned repository, without pinning a reviewed release or documenting integrity verification.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The instructions include deletion and export of potentially sensitive notes, but do not clearly warn that deletion can remove user data or that export can copy note contents outside Notes.app.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The artifact is a single Markdown skill file and does not install background services, scheduled jobs, memory rules, startup hooks, or other persistence mechanisms.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The skill coherently describes Apple Notes management through the memo CLI, including listing, searching, creating, editing, deleting, moving, and exporting notes.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"note"}],"guidance":"Review this skill before installing. Only use it if you trust the memo CLI source, understand that Automation permission can expose and modify your Apple Notes, and are prepared to confirm destructive actions like note deletion carefully.","findings":"[SQP-2] expected: The delete command is part of the stated notes-management purpose and is interactive, but the artifact does not provide a clear destructive-action warning or confirmation guidance for an agentic workflow.\n[SQP-2] expected: Automation permission is necessary for Apple Notes control, but the artifact does not adequately explain the privacy impact of granting that access.\n[T08] expected: Using the memo CLI is central to the skill, but the install guidance relies on mutable third-party sources and an ambiguous manual install path without version pinning or integrity checks.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789013574519}}}}}